# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.8 (P-D8) / §7.11 scenario 5: `host.submit()` never settles (JEVCODE_FAULT=submit:hang).
# The window the audit found: `run: 'starting'` is set by the App but the controller has not set `thinkingPhase`
# and no engine exists, so `host.abort()` falls through all three branches and does nothing while `abortRun()` has
# already dispatched `run:aborting`. The watchdog names the exit after SUBMIT_WATCHDOG_MS, Esc cancels locally, and
# the SECOND Ctrl-C always ends the process. Run with JEVCODE_SUBMIT_WATCHDOG_MS=1500 so the scenario is seconds.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.3
send make the tests pass
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect has not answered in
sleep 0.3
send \x1b
sleep 0.5
send \x03
sleep 0.3
send \x03
eof
